### Module 12 — Foundry-hosted Responses agent (local testing)
# These requests hit the agent running locally via `dotnet run` (or `docker run`)
# on http://localhost:8088. Running locally needs no auth — just POST to the
# Responses endpoint.
#
# For testing the agent once it's DEPLOYED to Foundry, use the azd commands
# instead of raw HTTP — they handle auth for you (no token minting required).
# See the "Testing the deployed agent" note at the bottom of this file.

@host = http://localhost:8088
@path = /responses
@agent = trip-planner

# Foundry's hosting layer scopes sessions by these two headers. In production
# Foundry sets them per user/conversation; locally you pick any stable strings.
# Without them the server returns HTTP 500 (isolation key provider returns null).
# Change @chatKey when you want to start a fresh conversation.
@userKey = local-dev-user
@chatKey = local-dev-chat

### 1. Simple request
POST {{host}}{{path}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-agent-user-isolation-key: {{userKey}}
x-agent-chat-isolation-key: {{chatKey}}

{
  "input": "Plan a 3-day trip to Tokyo in cherry blossom season.",
  "model": "{{agent}}"
}

### 2. Continue the conversation
# Pass the previous response.id in `previous_response_id` to keep the
# server-side conversation state going (the Responses-protocol equivalent of
# Module 10's `contextId`).
POST {{host}}{{path}}
Content-Type: application/json
x-agent-user-isolation-key: {{userKey}}
x-agent-chat-isolation-key: {{chatKey}}

{
  "input": "What about vegetarian options for that trip?",
  "model": "{{agent}}",
  "previous_response_id": "<paste id from a previous response here>"
}

###############################################################################
# Testing the deployed agent
#
# Once the agent is deployed to Foundry, don't hand-craft HTTP requests — the
# cloud endpoint requires an Entra token and a preview feature header. Use the
# azd commands instead; they resolve the endpoint and auth automatically:
#
#   # one-shot invoke (auto-detects the agent from azure.yaml)
#   azd ai agent invoke "Plan a 3-day trip to Tokyo in cherry blossom season."
#
#   # show agent details / current version / endpoint
#   azd ai agent show
#
#   # stream live logs from the hosted agent
#   azd ai agent monitor
###############################################################################
